Nature is the beautiful and essential world around us that supports all life on Earth. It encompasses everything from the vast oceans and towering mountains to the smallest insects and towering forests. Beyond its breathtaking landscapes, nature provides humanity with the fundamental resources required to survive, including clean air to breathe, fresh water to drink, and fertile soil to grow food. Spending time in natural environments also has a profound impact on human well-being, helping to reduce stress and inspire creativity. However, modern human activities like pollution and deforestation threaten this delicate global ecosystem. Protecting nature is not just about preserving scenery; it is an urgent responsibility to ensure a healthy, balanced planet for future generations.
